/*
  ceremonies/phishing/identity_strong.spthy -- the STRONG identity interface (ROADMAP #5; the #2 fix).
  The human forms its belief ONLY from a VERIFIED binding (the claim must match a credential bound to the
  channel) -- the anti-spoofing affordance. Under a spoofed presentation there is no Verified(_, adversary),
  so the false belief cannot form: the Attentive human does not proceed, and the secret never leaks.
*/

rule Believe_strong:
    [ Claimed('Alex', c), Channel('Alex', ch), Verified(c, ch) ]
  --[ Believes('Alex', c, 'strong') ]->
    [ Belief('Alex', c, ch) ]
